WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.243 --> 00:00:04.947
[MUSIC]

00:00:04.947 --> 00:00:07.446
Hello, and welcome to our conference call,

00:00:07.446 --> 00:00:11.430
MBA Admissions Insights: Considering
a Joint or Dual Degree.

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:12.830
Thanks for joining us.

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:17.040
My name is Allison Davis, I'm Associate
Director in the MBA Admissions Office.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:21.380
And I'm joined by my colleague,
Mary Oleksy, Associate Director, Joint and

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:23.240
Dual Degree Programs.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.780
&gt;&gt; Hi, everyone.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:28.490
&gt;&gt; In the next 30 minutes we'll be
talking about what to keep in mind

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:32.180
as you consider pursuing a joint or
dual degree.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:35.070
We'll start by reviewing some
of your options as a joint or

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:39.130
dual degree student and then we'll
discuss some questions that you may find

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:44.330
worthwhile to ask yourself before
pursuing a joint or dual degree.

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:48.170
We'll wrap up by answering some of
the questions that you've all submitted

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:49.410
in advance.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:51.800
So Mary, let's start off with the basics.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:56.170
Most of this is on our website,
but let's review it here briefly.

00:00:56.170 --> 00:01:00.600
To begin, can you tell us the difference
between a joint degree and a dual degree?

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:06.350
&gt;&gt; Yes, so in a joint degree
there's a reduction MBA units and

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:11.320
some MBA units may either be double
counted toward both degrees or

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:13.870
counted towards the other degree.

00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:15.908
In order to graduate with a joint degree,

00:01:15.908 --> 00:01:18.774
a student needs to meet both
sets of degree requirements.

00:01:18.774 --> 00:01:23.588
And I want to note that it takes
an additional one to three quarters beyond

00:01:23.588 --> 00:01:26.006
the two years for the standard MBA.

00:01:26.006 --> 00:01:30.923
In contrast, a dual degree program is when
a student pursues a second degree with any

00:01:30.923 --> 00:01:35.286
other graduate program at Stanford
University that we don't have a formal

00:01:35.286 --> 00:01:37.040
agreement with.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:39.730
There is a reduction in MBA units.

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:44.220
And this allows a student to start earning
credit towards their other degree program.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:47.110
I want to note that there's no
double counting of units, and

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:51.900
students complete the MBA in two years
when they complete a dual degree.

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:54.460
&gt;&gt; And there are even more options, right?

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:59.220
&gt;&gt; Yes, so beyond what's offered
at Stanford, students may also

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:04.080
pursue degrees with selected professional
schools at other universities.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:08.740
Right now, our list includes Public
Policy Programs at Harvard, Princeton and

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:13.520
Johns Hopkins along with the Harvard
Medical School, Yale Law School and

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:16.579
Yale Medical School, and
all of these are listed on our website.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:22.236
I want to note that we don't have formal
dual degree agreements with these schools.

00:02:22.236 --> 00:02:27.690
But we do partner with them informally
to offer these as study opportunities.

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:29.580
And what does this mean for you?

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:33.330
It means you need to do the leg work for
these dual study opportunities.

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:36.634
You will need to inquire with each
school regarding its policy and

00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:38.870
its timeline for the programs.

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:43.580
&gt;&gt; And why would somebody typically
be interested in pursuing

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:45.378
more than just an MBA?

00:02:45.378 --> 00:02:49.619
&gt;&gt; I think in today's complex world
there's more and more recognition

00:02:49.619 --> 00:02:53.859
of the intersection and interplay
of business with fields like law,

00:02:53.859 --> 00:02:58.180
education, technology and
medicine just to name a few.

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:03.038
Therefore, we know a students interests
and goals may span multiple disciplines.

00:03:03.038 --> 00:03:06.400
And we want to nurture that
by providing flexibility and

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:10.840
an opportunity to simultaneously
explore other academic areas.

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:13.920
So it may be helpful to know
that 21% of our current MBA

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:17.230
students are pursuing a joint or
a dual degree.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:21.310
&gt;&gt; And be aware also that there
are specific application instructions

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:25.110
depending on what type of joint or
dual degree you're interested in.

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:30.480
For example, for the JD/MBA, the MD/MBA,
the joint Master's in Computer Science and

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:35.580
a few others, you would use SAB,
which asks, why Stanford, in

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:41.610
the online MBA application to support your
rationale for the joint or dual degree.

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:45.240
While, for the joint Master's
in Education, you're required to

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:50.380
upload a personal statement in the joint
degrees section of the MBA application.

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:53.350
Again, all this information
is on our website, but

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:56.900
you should be aware of some of
these differences ahead of time.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:59.398
&gt;&gt; That's absolutely right.

00:03:59.398 --> 00:04:03.223
Again, I encourage you all to read
our website, the GSB website,

00:04:03.223 --> 00:04:06.980
as well as the website of the other
program you are interested in,

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:10.894
because there are specific
instructions depending on the degree.

00:04:10.894 --> 00:04:13.794
And in many cases,
you need to apply separately and

00:04:13.794 --> 00:04:16.190
you need to be admitted to both programs.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:17.201
So for example,

00:04:17.201 --> 00:04:22.220
our JD/MBA program with the Stanford
Law School falls into this category.

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:26.490
And then, in other cases such as
the joint Master's degree in Education,

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:28.360
we will forward your application and

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:31.260
personal statement to
the graduate school education.

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:34.300
So please do your homework and
read the website.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:37.400
&gt;&gt; There may also be
different tests required.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:41.970
For example,
the MBA program accepts both the GRE or

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:46.230
the GMAT, but the School of Engineering
will only accept the GRE for

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:50.750
Master's degree programs in computer
science and electrical engineering.

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:54.500
And if you're applying as
an international student,

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:58.816
the MBA program will accept the TOEFL,
the PTE, or the IELTS,

00:04:58.816 --> 00:05:02.988
while the School of Engineering
will only accept the TOEFL.

00:05:02.988 --> 00:05:05.220
&gt;&gt; Yes, all correct.

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:09.490
And again, specific requirements for each
program are listed on the web sites and so

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:12.560
you just want to make sure
you're familiar with that.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:16.730
&gt;&gt; Mary, I think we should also mention
that applicants should be mindful of

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:17.960
when to apply.

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:20.760
The MBA program has three
application rounds,

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:25.990
with deadlines this year on September 21,
January 10, and April 5.

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:31.140
However, other degree programs may only
have one application deadline, typically,

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:32.668
in mid-December.

00:05:32.668 --> 00:05:33.750
The reply date,

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:38.890
which is the date by which you must accept
your offered admission, may also vary.

00:05:38.890 --> 00:05:43.040
So you don't want to find yourself in
a situation where you have to decide if

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:46.570
you're accepting your offer of
admission to one degree program

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:50.890
before you know if you've gotten
into the other degree program.

00:05:50.890 --> 00:05:53.720
&gt;&gt; Yeah,
I really appreciate you highlighting that.

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:56.640
If you're applying, for example,
to the computer science or

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:59.410
electrical engineering
joined degree programs,

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:03.450
I really recommend that you apply
to the MBA program in round two.

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:05.400
So again,
this is something to be aware of.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:09.692
You want to make sure you check for each
degree program, not only the application

00:06:09.692 --> 00:06:13.970
deadlines but also the date that you'll
receive your admission decision and

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:17.179
the dates where you must accept or
decline your offer of admission.

00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:22.116
&gt;&gt; Mary, let's talk about what's your
role in working with students who

00:06:22.116 --> 00:06:24.893
are interested in pursuing a joint or
dual degree.

00:06:24.893 --> 00:06:29.630
&gt;&gt; Mm-hm, so I work with both current
students and admitted students.

00:06:29.630 --> 00:06:33.260
For currently enrolled students,
I provide academic advising and

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:36.340
support with navigating
both degree programs.

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:40.810
I also offer general advising sessions for
admits and students who are considering

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:44.910
applying for a joint or dual degree and
want to talk through those options.

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:49.230
&gt;&gt; And just to be clear, you work
only with MBA students once they're

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:53.850
admitted to the MBA program, and
with current students who are pursuing or

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:56.530
are interested in
pursuing a second degree,

00:06:56.530 --> 00:07:01.140
your role is not to advise applicants or
prospective applicants.

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:04.720
&gt;&gt; Yeah, [LAUGH] sorry, that is correct,
I only work with admits and students.

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:11.180
&gt;&gt; All right,
now why don't we back up for a moment and

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:15.828
talk about some questions that
you out there should be asking

00:07:15.828 --> 00:07:20.500
yourselves as you're getting ready
to apply for joint or dual degree.

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:22.354
Answering these questions for

00:07:22.354 --> 00:07:26.282
yourself now can save you time
later in the application process.

00:07:26.282 --> 00:07:29.835
So, of course, first you need
to ask yourself, is a joint or

00:07:29.835 --> 00:07:31.630
dual degree right for you?

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:34.613
And how would you suggest
people think about that, Mary?

00:07:34.613 --> 00:07:39.532
&gt;&gt; Mm-hm, yeah, and this is important
to spend some time thinking about and

00:07:39.532 --> 00:07:42.200
I suggest that you start at a high level.

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:46.260
So let's start with a vision, and
I know that this is going to change for

00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:50.393
you many times but, what is your
vision today for your future career?

00:07:50.393 --> 00:07:55.119
And do those career dreams include
opportunities or roles where a specific

00:07:55.119 --> 00:07:59.994
degree beyond an MBA is either required
for you to get your foot in the door or Or

00:07:59.994 --> 00:08:04.211
to be successful in that position,
so you want to think about that.

00:08:04.211 --> 00:08:08.690
Another thing to think about is how
important is having those letters and

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:10.830
answer the MA asked you your name?

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:13.280
Sometimes it matters and
sometimes it doesn't.

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:16.350
If the MA or
the MS letters asked you your name or

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:20.440
not as important you want to think about,
what's the content, the experience,

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:24.290
or the context that you need to learn
in order to pursue your vision?

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:30.255
I would also spend some time reflecting
on what you hope to gain from

00:08:30.255 --> 00:08:33.588
pursuing an MBA and
from pursuing a joint degree.

00:08:33.588 --> 00:08:37.446
And is there room in this vision you have
of what your MBA is going to be like for

00:08:37.446 --> 00:08:41.367
the trade offs that you're going to need
to make when you're pursuing a joint

00:08:41.367 --> 00:08:45.787
of duel degree program, because there are
some choices that you'll have to make and

00:08:45.787 --> 00:08:48.440
you can't say yes to everything.

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:51.570
You also want to think about, are you at
a place in your life where you can make

00:08:51.570 --> 00:08:55.480
the time and the financial commitment
to stay for additional quarters beyond

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:59.740
the two years required for the MBA,
because that can be significant.

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:00.763
So do you have personal or

00:09:00.763 --> 00:09:04.148
family commitments that you need to
consider when you're making this decision?

00:09:04.148 --> 00:09:07.330
But I think all those are important
high level questions to think about.

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:09.050
&gt;&gt; Great.

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:12.930
Next, how do I decide which joint or
dual degree to apply to?

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:18.830
&gt;&gt; Yeah, we have a lot of
interesting programs here.

00:09:18.830 --> 00:09:21.530
And so,
I think once you have a clear sense of

00:09:21.530 --> 00:09:25.390
what's the subject area that you're
interested in, go do your homework.

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:28.940
I would do some research and
deeply explore both the structure and

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:31.350
the course requirements of the program.

00:09:31.350 --> 00:09:34.600
And the question to notice,
when you read through these classes,

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:36.860
do you feel excited about it?

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:40.490
Maybe not every single class, but
you want to test for a sense of alignment

00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:45.160
between the program offerings and
your learning goals, so trust your gut.

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:48.840
Something else you want to think about
is your competitiveness as an applicant,

00:09:48.840 --> 00:09:52.800
so in general I believe you should
always throw your hat in the ring for

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:55.420
a degree program that
you're interested in.

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:58.050
That being said as with
the MBA applications.

00:09:58.050 --> 00:10:00.590
Location, it can also be
a significant time commitment

00:10:00.590 --> 00:10:04.430
to pull together a compelling application
for a joint or a dual degree.

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:08.730
It can take hours to prepare for the
exams, requesting recommendation letters,

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:11.790
or writing your responses
to an essay question.

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:15.640
So if it's available, I would take
a look at the admissions criteria or

00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:19.410
the statistics for the student body
of the program you're interested in.

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:21.711
To assess, are you a viable candidate for

00:10:21.711 --> 00:10:24.684
this program and
would this be a good use of your time?

00:10:24.684 --> 00:10:27.918
And I want to highlight that
the advantage of doing a joint or

00:10:27.918 --> 00:10:31.680
dual degree program is that you're
going to blend your learning and

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:36.160
you're going to be more efficient with
your time and financial resources.

00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:40.540
But the challenge is that you have
to prioritize and make some choice.

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:44.591
Around what is it that you're coming
here to learn, what's the experience you

00:10:44.591 --> 00:10:48.044
want to have and how can you fit that
into allotted time that you have.

00:10:48.044 --> 00:10:49.278
&gt;&gt; Great, good advice.

00:10:49.278 --> 00:10:54.247
People should also think about timing and
ask themselves, should I apply for

00:10:54.247 --> 00:10:57.687
a joint redo if degree while
I'm applying for an MBA or

00:10:57.687 --> 00:11:01.380
wait until I'm already
student at Stanford.

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:03.250
&gt;&gt; It's an interesting question.

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:08.213
So if your decision to come to Stanford
depends on being accepted to both degree

00:11:08.213 --> 00:11:12.890
programs, then you need to apply for
those both in advance of enrolling.

00:11:12.890 --> 00:11:17.274
But if you're not totally sure, and you
want to do this Stanford MBA regardless of

00:11:17.274 --> 00:11:21.012
what are you are accepted into a second
degree program you can wait and

00:11:21.012 --> 00:11:25.330
you could wait in apply during your first
year at the Business School to the other

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:28.420
degree program and
then make your decision.

00:11:28.420 --> 00:11:33.000
&gt;&gt; How many students do apply
after they're already here?

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:37.620
About half of our students
pursuing a second degree do that.

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:38.570
So 50/50.

00:11:38.570 --> 00:11:42.510
And just as a reminder, the application
requirements like test scores,

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:47.250
essays, etc., all of those things are
the same whether you apply in advance or

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:49.450
whether or
you wait until once you're a student here.

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:55.380
&gt;&gt; Last, if I'm accepted to a joint or
dual degree, how does the timing work,

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:58.400
which program should I start first,
do I even have a choice?

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:01.472
&gt;&gt; So my famous answer, it depends.

00:12:01.472 --> 00:12:02.240
[LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:04.770
&gt;&gt; It depends on, and I would refer you to

00:12:04.770 --> 00:12:09.530
the website, to our website to see
kind of the pathways and options, for

00:12:09.530 --> 00:12:13.510
example medical school students
always start at the med school and

00:12:13.510 --> 00:12:16.660
most JD-MBAs start at the law school.

00:12:16.660 --> 00:12:21.010
Other programs such as E-IPER,
the masters in public policy or

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:25.380
the MA in education, all those
students will start at the GSB first.

00:12:25.380 --> 00:12:27.610
For programs like
electrical engineering and

00:12:27.610 --> 00:12:30.120
computer science,
it's more of a personal preference.

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:32.280
So where do you wish to start?

00:12:32.280 --> 00:12:34.158
&gt;&gt; Great, Mary.

00:12:34.158 --> 00:12:38.509
Let's move on now to answering audience
questions and again thanks to so

00:12:38.509 --> 00:12:41.930
many of you for
submitting questions in advance.

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:45.920
So first question, what are the financial
aid opportunities for joint and

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:51.340
dual degree students and how do they
differ from regular MBA students?

00:12:51.340 --> 00:12:53.980
&gt;&gt; Yeah, this is a really good question.

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:55.810
So for students pursuing a joint or

00:12:55.810 --> 00:12:59.330
dual degree here at Stanford,
you're treated the same

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:04.660
as an MBA-only student when it comes to
determining financial aid eligibility.

00:13:04.660 --> 00:13:09.470
Financial aid here is awarded based on
need, and one thing to think about is,

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:14.798
depending on which degree you're pursuing,
it may be best to start at the GSB first,

00:13:14.798 --> 00:13:18.794
as we will provide financial aid,
including fellowships, for

00:13:18.794 --> 00:13:22.352
the entire time it takes to
complete your joint degrees.

00:13:22.352 --> 00:13:25.940
This is a discussion you can have in more
detail with our Financial Aid Office after

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:27.039
you've been admitted.

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:32.260
Let me also note, for those of you
considering study opportunities

00:13:32.260 --> 00:13:35.230
outside of Stanford, you are eligible for

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:41.090
financial aid from Stanford only during
the time that you are here for the MBA.

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:43.830
And so, the other institution
would be responsible for

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:47.410
any financial aid you're receiving
while you're attending their program.

00:13:47.410 --> 00:13:48.780
And so,
you would need to apply separately.

00:13:48.780 --> 00:13:51.220
Lead for
financial aid in that institution.

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:52.480
&gt;&gt; Right.

00:13:52.480 --> 00:13:57.480
Are most joint degree students people
who study related fields in undergrad?

00:13:58.550 --> 00:14:00.556
&gt;&gt; So not necessarily.

00:14:00.556 --> 00:14:04.172
Our technical degree programs like
computer science and electrical

00:14:04.172 --> 00:14:08.410
engineering tend to have the most direct
correlation between undergraduate and

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:10.090
graduate experience.

00:14:10.090 --> 00:14:14.210
But other programs such as education,
E-IPER, or

00:14:14.210 --> 00:14:19.800
public policy, all have a broader
spectrum of undergraduate backgrounds.

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:24.790
&gt;&gt; Will schools confer with each other
during the joint degree admission process?

00:14:24.790 --> 00:14:26.880
&gt;&gt; Allison,
I'm going to defer that one to you.

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:27.670
&gt;&gt; Okay, sure.

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:31.300
The admission decisions
are made separately.

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:35.460
We do on our application
form if you have applied or

00:14:35.460 --> 00:14:39.520
are considering applying to
a joint degree and which degree.

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:43.020
So we are aware that you may
have applied to another program.

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:46.215
For dual degrees students
need to apply and

00:14:46.215 --> 00:14:51.640
be accepted to the other program
separately and then notify our office.

00:14:51.640 --> 00:14:56.540
In any case, if you're admitted to the MBA
program and any second degree program,

00:14:56.540 --> 00:15:00.950
whether it's a joint or dual degree at
Stanford or one of the selected study

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:06.201
opportunities outside Stanford, Mary, will
be available to answer your questions and

00:15:06.201 --> 00:15:10.359
help you map out your schedule of
how you'll pursue the two programs.

00:15:11.990 --> 00:15:16.540
Next question, are there specific
number of spots available for

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:18.690
each Joint or Dual Degree program?

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:24.240
&gt;&gt; There are some programs that
have MBA specific cohorts.

00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:26.207
So in particular education and

00:15:26.207 --> 00:15:31.920
E-IPER will typically accept
approximately 20 to 25 students each year

00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:35.940
The cohorts for the other programs are
really based on who they want to accept.

00:15:35.940 --> 00:15:37.710
So there is no set number.

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:43.785
&gt;&gt; Can you discuss the computer
science joint degree and

00:15:43.785 --> 00:15:49.925
the various careers that people who have
graduated with that degree get into?

00:15:49.925 --> 00:15:52.781
&gt;&gt; The CS joint degree is a young program.

00:15:52.781 --> 00:15:55.846
We're going into our
third year of existence.

00:15:55.846 --> 00:15:59.965
And in speaking with our current students
there is something I want to highlight for

00:15:59.965 --> 00:16:00.730
all of you.

00:16:00.730 --> 00:16:04.210
So students tell me this
is not a program for

00:16:04.210 --> 00:16:06.920
students interested in
being product managers.

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:10.374
What this is, is a program for
students who wish to

00:16:10.374 --> 00:16:14.914
take a deeper dive into a specific
area within computer science.

00:16:14.914 --> 00:16:19.458
So I would advise you, if you're thinking
about this program, please, go explore

00:16:19.458 --> 00:16:23.811
the computer science website and take a
close look at the areas of specialization

00:16:23.811 --> 00:16:28.980
because you want to make sure that what
they're offering matches your interests.

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:33.390
And regarding careers, we actually only
have one graduate of the program at

00:16:33.390 --> 00:16:37.069
this point, so I don't really have data
yet to share about the career path.

00:16:38.230 --> 00:16:40.580
&gt;&gt; And Mary,
would should also probably mention,

00:16:40.580 --> 00:16:44.390
in terms of undergraduate backgrounds for

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:49.570
computer science, they really do need
to have a technical undergrad degree.

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:50.630
Is that right?

00:16:50.630 --> 00:16:53.230
&gt;&gt; Yeah, they should be highly
quantitative or technical.

00:16:53.230 --> 00:16:59.430
So computer science, applied math,
engineering at something in that genre.

00:16:59.430 --> 00:17:02.620
&gt;&gt; Or physics I guess is one
that I think is acceptable.

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:04.930
So again, take a look at their website.

00:17:04.930 --> 00:17:07.266
But they are looking for people with,

00:17:07.266 --> 00:17:12.385
to be competitive applicant you do need to
have a technical under graduate degree.

00:17:12.385 --> 00:17:13.530
Next question.

00:17:13.530 --> 00:17:18.816
If I join a joint or dual degree program,
will I later be able to drop one and

00:17:18.816 --> 00:17:24.045
focus on the other or do I have to
follow through with both no matter what?

00:17:24.045 --> 00:17:24.980
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:27.890
This is also like a it depends question.

00:17:27.890 --> 00:17:31.250
But let me say in general,
it's a difficult position to be and

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:35.720
if you're in a joint degree program and
you're not sure if this is the right path,

00:17:35.720 --> 00:17:39.200
and that's why doing your homework now,
on alignment and

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:43.710
program fit is so
important and in general,

00:17:43.710 --> 00:17:49.400
if a program is no longer a fit it's
likely you would be able to withdraw.

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:53.490
However, depending on the timing there can
be significant implication on your degree

00:17:53.490 --> 00:17:58.690
progress and graduating in time so this
is a decision to be made carefully and

00:17:58.690 --> 00:18:03.280
is definitely a decision that students
would consult with me before making.

00:18:03.280 --> 00:18:07.630
&gt;&gt; And I think this might be an example of
a situation where you might wait to apply

00:18:07.630 --> 00:18:09.900
once you're already
an MBA student here and

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:13.360
you kind of get the lay of the land and
what the work load is and

00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:16.890
then apply as a first year student
to that other degree program.

00:18:16.890 --> 00:18:17.670
&gt;&gt; Yeah, I agree.

00:18:18.820 --> 00:18:21.730
&gt;&gt; How demanding is it
to take a dual degree

00:18:21.730 --> 00:18:24.720
if the second degree is
from Stanford also and

00:18:24.720 --> 00:18:29.660
this person is thinking of the MA in
either education or public policy?

00:18:31.480 --> 00:18:36.415
&gt;&gt; So I want to delineate a difference
between demanding versus commitment and

00:18:36.415 --> 00:18:38.370
challenging.

00:18:38.370 --> 00:18:43.740
So taking on a second degree, it's
a commitment, and if you're fully aware of

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:49.100
the ramifications of that choice in the
beginning, it shouldn't be a painful one.

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:51.000
&gt;From an academic perspective,

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:56.150
all of our students have been academically
successful in our joint degree programs.

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:59.250
So what you're really navigating
in regards to demanding or

00:18:59.250 --> 00:19:03.210
challenging is what electives
are you going to take when and

00:19:03.210 --> 00:19:06.300
how do you spend your time outside of
the classroom when you have homework,

00:19:06.300 --> 00:19:09.760
class preparation and
other activities that you want to do.

00:19:09.760 --> 00:19:12.250
So it's really more around
priority management,

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:17.000
time management,
then it is about like overall demanding.

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:20.560
&gt;&gt; What about the more technical
degrees like electrical engineering or

00:19:20.560 --> 00:19:22.790
computer science, how demanding are they?

00:19:22.790 --> 00:19:23.710
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:19:23.710 --> 00:19:29.560
Those I would consider more demanding,
especially in regards to time.

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:34.090
So for example students have shared
with me that one class can sometimes

00:19:34.090 --> 00:19:36.775
be 20 to 25 hours of work
outside of the classroom.

00:19:36.775 --> 00:19:37.355
&gt;&gt; Wow.

00:19:37.355 --> 00:19:39.543
&gt;&gt; So this is not a degree for
the faint of heart.

00:19:39.543 --> 00:19:41.162
[LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Right, okay.

00:19:41.162 --> 00:19:45.905
May I apply to a joint degree after
being accepted to the MBA program?

00:19:45.905 --> 00:19:50.195
Is it more competitive than applying
to the regular MBA program?

00:19:50.195 --> 00:19:54.370
&gt;&gt; So I think we've spoken to this
already that yes, you can apply after.

00:19:54.370 --> 00:19:59.520
And it is not more competitive than
when you're applying during the MBA

00:19:59.520 --> 00:20:04.670
initial cycle, as mentioned earlier,mother
application requirements are all the same,

00:20:04.670 --> 00:20:06.000
regardless when you apply.

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:13.360
&gt;&gt; For programs that require travel
between two universities, how

00:20:13.360 --> 00:20:17.970
well can students really create a strong
connection to the Stanford community.

00:20:19.010 --> 00:20:22.210
&gt;&gt; So when we talk about connection to
the community, I think what we're really

00:20:22.210 --> 00:20:27.050
talking about are student relationships,
and from what I have seen, students have

00:20:27.050 --> 00:20:31.690
been able to maintain a strong sense of
connection through these relationships.

00:20:31.690 --> 00:20:35.200
What I also notice is students
tend to be fully immersed and

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:37.660
present in their actual location.

00:20:37.660 --> 00:20:40.800
So if they're here at the GSB,
they're fully here at the GSB and

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:43.350
the same is true for the other program.

00:20:43.350 --> 00:20:47.587
And so, if you're at your other
institution you're taking full advantage

00:20:47.587 --> 00:20:50.232
of the resources and
the people that are there,

00:20:50.232 --> 00:20:53.626
so I don't think you have the same
sense of missing out here.

00:20:53.626 --> 00:20:59.100
And all of our students still have access
to the all the GSB's online resources and

00:20:59.100 --> 00:21:03.770
also staff are available to connect
over the phone or video chat.

00:21:03.770 --> 00:21:08.540
So I think students can remain as
connected to the GSB as they want to be.

00:21:08.540 --> 00:21:13.420
&gt;&gt; Students have told me that it's really
a chance to enlarge their own community

00:21:13.420 --> 00:21:16.750
and they pretty much end up sort
of doubling their network at

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:21.060
not only two different universities but
two different departments on campus.

00:21:22.450 --> 00:21:27.410
&gt;&gt; Another question here, I would love
to learn more about how distinct or

00:21:27.410 --> 00:21:33.490
integrated we should make the applications
especially with regard to the essays,

00:21:33.490 --> 00:21:37.290
is some overlap in our
responses to the essays.

00:21:38.890 --> 00:21:40.980
I'll go ahead and answer that one.

00:21:40.980 --> 00:21:46.110
MBA Admissions only reads the two essays
that are required for our application and

00:21:46.110 --> 00:21:50.590
those are this year what matters most
to you and why, and why Stanford.

00:21:50.590 --> 00:21:55.080
We would expect that you would address
your interest, and your rationale for

00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:58.310
the second degree in the Y Stanford essay.

00:21:58.310 --> 00:22:03.220
The other degree program typically
does not have access to or

00:22:03.220 --> 00:22:06.150
read the essays required for the MBA.

00:22:06.150 --> 00:22:10.409
So yes there will of course be
some overlap in the essays,

00:22:10.409 --> 00:22:13.264
as they're for a separate audience.

00:22:13.264 --> 00:22:18.184
I'm not quite sure if this person is
asking how much overlap there could

00:22:18.184 --> 00:22:22.940
be between the two MBA essays,
the what matters most to you and why and

00:22:22.940 --> 00:22:27.070
the why Stanford,
that's really entirely up to you.

00:22:27.070 --> 00:22:30.270
Both essays are read by
the MBA admissions office.

00:22:30.270 --> 00:22:33.890
How distinct or
integrated the two essays are, of course,

00:22:33.890 --> 00:22:36.000
depends on what you're writing about.

00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:40.320
So for example, if what matters most
to you relates to your reasons for

00:22:40.320 --> 00:22:45.000
pursuing two degrees, there could
be a real overlap in the topic.

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:48.120
If what most matters most to you
is distinct from your interest in

00:22:48.120 --> 00:22:51.600
the two degrees,
there may be no overlap in the essays.

00:22:53.240 --> 00:22:56.124
Here's a question about JD-MBA.

00:22:56.124 --> 00:23:01.340
For JD-MBAs, students,
do you have enough time to establish

00:23:01.340 --> 00:23:06.120
strong relationships with both your GSB
and Stanford Law School classmates?

00:23:06.120 --> 00:23:10.160
Which we sort of addressed, but
any further comments there Mary?

00:23:10.160 --> 00:23:12.120
&gt;&gt; Yeah, I would just say, yes.

00:23:12.120 --> 00:23:13.665
Yes, there is time.

00:23:13.665 --> 00:23:17.471
In part because students typically
spend one full year, at least,

00:23:17.471 --> 00:23:19.460
immersed at the law school.

00:23:19.460 --> 00:23:22.350
And then,
another full year immersed at the GSB.

00:23:22.350 --> 00:23:25.920
So you are able to connect
with your colleagues.

00:23:25.920 --> 00:23:29.710
And I think right in the blended years is
where it's a little bit more challenging.

00:23:29.710 --> 00:23:34.300
Because you have two communities and
two full sets of activities as options.

00:23:35.990 --> 00:23:38.710
&gt;&gt; Here's a question about
Masters in Education.

00:23:38.710 --> 00:23:43.372
Can I apply separately to the MBA and
the MA in Education so

00:23:43.372 --> 00:23:49.610
in case I'm not admitted to the GSB,
I can still pursue the MA in Education?

00:23:49.610 --> 00:23:53.477
If I am able to apply
separately the same year, and

00:23:53.477 --> 00:23:58.649
I am admitted to both degrees,
can I pursue them as a joint degree.

00:23:58.649 --> 00:24:00.389
&gt;&gt; This is a good nuanced question.

00:24:00.389 --> 00:24:03.847
So the MA in education,
MBA program is only for

00:24:03.847 --> 00:24:07.730
students who are admitted
to both programs.

00:24:07.730 --> 00:24:11.903
So if you are not accepted to the GSB, you
would need to apply to a different program

00:24:11.903 --> 00:24:16.139
at the graduate school of education and I
would encourage you to visit their website

00:24:16.139 --> 00:24:19.066
as they'll have more information
on the on the options.

00:24:19.066 --> 00:24:24.529
&gt;&gt; Another common question we get, Mary
about school of education is if the joint

00:24:24.529 --> 00:24:29.690
masters with education includes
a teaching credential and it does not.

00:24:29.690 --> 00:24:30.306
Correct?

00:24:30.306 --> 00:24:31.930
&gt;&gt; Yes, that is correct.

00:24:31.930 --> 00:24:35.150
Although the graduate school of
education offers a teaching credential,

00:24:35.150 --> 00:24:37.667
it is not part of
the joint master's Program.

00:24:39.210 --> 00:24:43.370
&gt;&gt; We'll pursuing a dual
degree burnout students and

00:24:43.370 --> 00:24:46.910
this student is interested in MS and
Computer Science.

00:24:48.380 --> 00:24:50.662
&gt;&gt; So,
let's talk about what causes burnout.

00:24:50.662 --> 00:24:51.442
In my mind,

00:24:51.442 --> 00:24:56.436
burnout is taking on too much without
the resources to make it sustainable.

00:24:56.436 --> 00:25:01.498
So yes, the computer science degree
program requires extensive hours outside

00:25:01.498 --> 00:25:06.255
of the classroom and that means that you
need to be willing to prioritize and

00:25:06.255 --> 00:25:09.746
make trade-offs in order
to find a sustainable path.

00:25:09.746 --> 00:25:11.923
But again, I spoke about this earlier.

00:25:11.923 --> 00:25:16.736
If there's alignment between the program
and your goals, then there's a connection.

00:25:16.736 --> 00:25:19.350
And so, those trade-offs shouldn't
be too difficult to make.

00:25:20.480 --> 00:25:24.161
&gt;&gt; For students who are interested
in doing both the MA and

00:25:24.161 --> 00:25:29.042
a Master's in Public Policy at Stanford
is less than the current average

00:25:29.042 --> 00:25:33.779
work experience for an MBA,
which is four years average acceptable.

00:25:33.779 --> 00:25:36.836
So if somebody has three years or
two years, is that okay?

00:25:36.836 --> 00:25:39.989
This is admissions questions,
again, I'll take that.

00:25:39.989 --> 00:25:44.607
There is no requirement for
the number of years work experience for

00:25:44.607 --> 00:25:49.650
the MBA program or for any joint or
dual degree program, as far as I know.

00:25:51.570 --> 00:25:54.810
How many students per
year pursue a degree with

00:25:54.810 --> 00:25:58.890
a Harvard Kennedy School concurrently
with an MBA from the GSB?

00:25:58.890 --> 00:26:04.651
And if somebody is applying to
the MBA program in this coming cycle,

00:26:04.651 --> 00:26:08.503
would they be applying to start in 2018?

00:26:08.503 --> 00:26:13.748
&gt;&gt; We have approximately 10 to 15 students
each year that are doing the program

00:26:13.748 --> 00:26:18.994
with the Harvard Kennedy School and a
recommendation in regards to applying for

00:26:18.994 --> 00:26:24.600
the GSB is that you should be applying for
the year that you wish to start.

00:26:24.600 --> 00:26:29.003
&gt;&gt; And so, somebody would apply to
Harvard Kennedy this coming cycle

00:26:29.003 --> 00:26:31.603
and then-
&gt;&gt; They should wait until next year to

00:26:31.603 --> 00:26:32.870
apply to the GSB.

00:26:32.870 --> 00:26:34.123
&gt;&gt; Okay, got it.

00:26:34.123 --> 00:26:39.083
What have graduates of Stanford's joint
masters education accomplished as

00:26:39.083 --> 00:26:41.890
a result of their experience at Stanford?

00:26:41.890 --> 00:26:47.314
&gt;&gt; So I think what you're asking here is
what careers have these student gone onto,

00:26:47.314 --> 00:26:49.968
let me give you a sampling of the areas.

00:26:49.968 --> 00:26:52.510
They've gone into tech startups.

00:26:52.510 --> 00:26:56.642
International schools,
charter schools, higher education,

00:26:56.642 --> 00:27:00.632
administration and education investing,
just to name a few.

00:27:00.632 --> 00:27:03.895
&gt;&gt; Well, we're almost out of time.

00:27:03.895 --> 00:27:06.884
If you didn't get your
question answered today,

00:27:06.884 --> 00:27:11.590
please feel free to contact our office
by email or phone to ask your questions.

00:27:12.990 --> 00:27:17.470
Before we go, Mary, any words of
advice for our listeners today?

00:27:17.470 --> 00:27:22.600
&gt;&gt; Yeah, so I think pursuing a joint or
a dual degree can be a wonderful

00:27:22.600 --> 00:27:28.070
opportunity and it's something to be done
with purposeful reflection and intention.

00:27:29.100 --> 00:27:33.410
Given that for many of you coming to
graduate school is a one time occurrence,

00:27:33.410 --> 00:27:37.030
it really makes sense to be efficient
with your time, to maximize your

00:27:37.030 --> 00:27:40.849
interdisciplinary learning and
to make use of your financial resources.

00:27:42.160 --> 00:27:44.086
So, my best piece of advice for

00:27:44.086 --> 00:27:47.862
you is try to get as clear as you
can on what you want to learn and

00:27:47.862 --> 00:27:52.474
then just make sure that the program
you're applying to meets that need.

00:27:52.474 --> 00:27:55.406
So, your expectations are realistic and
aligned.

00:27:55.406 --> 00:27:56.790
And hopefully, they're met.

00:27:56.790 --> 00:27:58.150
Good luck on that.

00:27:58.150 --> 00:28:01.922
&gt;&gt; Thank you, Mary and thank you to
everyone out there for joining us.

00:28:01.922 --> 00:28:06.648
An audio recording of this conference call
will be posted on our website in the next

00:28:06.648 --> 00:28:07.640
few weeks.

00:28:07.640 --> 00:28:12.268
The previous three calls in our
MBA Admissions Insights series are already

00:28:12.268 --> 00:28:14.705
posted there, so take a look at those.

00:28:14.705 --> 00:28:18.270
The current application is
now available on our website.

00:28:18.270 --> 00:28:23.197
Again, there are three application
deadlines, September 21,

00:28:23.197 --> 00:28:25.193
January 10 and April 5.

00:28:25.193 --> 00:28:28.997
On our website,
you'll find videos of webinars and

00:28:28.997 --> 00:28:32.715
a calendar of events offered
both on an oncampus and

00:28:32.715 --> 00:28:37.870
around the world We look forward to
meeting you online or in person.

00:28:37.870 --> 00:28:38.490
Goodbye for now.

